    handbook: untrack the panel loop's runtime state
    
    The loop's STATE.json and per-round transcripts were tracked. A checkout/rebase then
    restored STATE.json to a committed snapshot while untracked round dirs disappeared, and
    the counter rewound 17 -> 12 with five rounds of work gone and no process left running.
    
    Round state is runtime, not source: it is gitignored now and stays on disk. The chapters
    remain tracked — they are the artifact. If a transcript must be kept for audit, snapshot
    it into docs/handbook/evidence/ deliberately, at a named revision.
