-│ +
-│ +## 2. Purpose
-│ +
-│ +**What breaks if this module is absent.** The whole control plane has no clock: no cadence
-│ +tick fires, so nothing is ever admitted, dispatched or settled. The scheduler is the source
-│ +of every admission decision (eligibility, tasks-vs-cooldown, board gates, fairness, budget
-│ +reservation — OUTLINE M9.S1).
-│ +
-│ +**What breaks if it lies.** A scheduler that records a pass for a `status:"failed"` reply is
-│ +the control-plane half of the silent-success defect (CF-355: it never reads the 12 result
-│ +fields). A scheduler that dispatches `text_b64` to a node that reads `text` dispatches work
-│ +that cannot run (CF-354).
-│ +
-│ +## 3. Dependencies and library contracts
